%description:

Tcp.initialWindow:rfc3390 -- the first flight has three segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the initial congestion window: "rfc2001" = 1 SMSS; "rfc3390" =
min(4*SMSS, max(2*SMSS, 4380 bytes)) [...]; "rfc6928" = min(10*SMSS, max(2*SMSS, 14600
bytes)), as Linux".

The classes: rfc2001 (one segment; LegacyTcp), rfc3390 (the default:
min(4*SMSS, max(2*SMSS, 4380 bytes)), 3 segments of 1448 bytes) and rfc6928 (LinuxTcp:
min(10*SMSS, max(2*SMSS, 14600 bytes)), 10 segments). The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::getInitialWindow(). This test separates "rfc3390" from the other two.

Host under test: host1, which sends 30000 bytes. Observation: level 1, the data segments that host1 sends before the first ACK of data comes
back: the links have a delay of 10 ms, so the round trip is 40 ms, and a full-sized segment
has 1448 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialWindow
%# class: rfc3390
%# value: "rfc3390"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialWindow
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpInitialWindowRfc3390")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("flight")
                                        .describe("each data segment of host1")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{flight} == 3")
             .describe("the first ACK of data, after 3 data segments")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialWindowRfc3390 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialWindow = "rfc3390"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 30000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpInitialWindowRfc3390: PASS
